# Ratcheted Trivy baseline. Policy:
#   - add an entry only for a finding that cannot be fixed in the repository;
#   - every entry carries the reason and the date it was reviewed;
#   - an entry dies with its finding — delete it the moment the code goes.
# Scan scope: HIGH/CRITICAL, fixed vulnerabilities only, vendored
# node_modules skipped (see .github/workflows/trivy.yml).

# DS-0002 — nginx/Dockerfile has no USER instruction. The official
# nginx:alpine image starts the master process as root so it can bind
# :80/:443, then drops privileges to the nginx user; the image entrypoint
# also generates the self-signed certificate and needs write access to the
# certificate paths. Forcing USER would break both. The backend image runs
# as a non-root user and passes this check today.
# Reviewed 2026-10-19 (Trivy 0.76.0).
DS-0002
